<title>USA: TABLE - Continental July load factor up.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Continental July load factor up.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997		  1996</p>
<p> Load factor - percent		  76.3		72.0</p>
<p> Revenue passenger miles	 4,546,989	 3,920,092</p>
<p> Available seat miles	    5,957,803	 5,446,805</p>
<p> Total cargo ton miles		49,038	    41,941</p>
<p>					    Year-to-date</p>
<p> Load factor - percent		  71.5		68.8</p>
<p> Revenue passenger miles	27,359,334	24,205,164</p>
<p> Available seat miles	   38,275,453	35,167,527</p>
<p> Total cargo ton miles	     317,815	   273,127</p>
<p>(Revenue passenger, available seat and total cargo ton miles in 000s)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Continental Airlines Inc.</p>
<p>The company's Continental Express unit's July load factor was 60.5 pct vs 54.4 pct.</p>
